#
# Worked example — the occurrent refinement (the YAMATO/Galton process-not-equal-event
# distinction) carried as VALUES and relations, not as rigid subclasses.
#
# Three things are shown for a single rocket launch:
#
#   1. The action(open)/event(closed) boundary as a VALUE (logic:occurrentBoundary).
#      The same occurrence is logic:Open while it unfolds (the launching, an on-going
#      action over an open interval) and a separate logic:Closed record once whole
#      (the launch, a completed unitary event over a closed interval). Boundedness is
#      an indexed value (Principle 9), not a rigid kind.
#
#   2. Causal parthood among occurrents (logic:causalPartOf). The ignition causally
#      contributes to the launch — every causal part is also a temporal part of the
#      same whole, but causal parthood is transitive WITHOUT being a strict order,
#      since causal feedback loops are legal among occurrents.
#
#   3. Constitution (logic:occurrentConstituent). The completed launch event is made
#      of the burning process — the change-stuff it is constituted by. Constitution is
#      NOT parthood: the process is not thereby asserted a temporal part of the event.
#
# A logic:Process MAY vary over its extent (it bears time-varying logic:Fluents); a
# completed logic:Closed event cannot — that change-asymmetry is the
# logic:OccurrentChangeAsymmetry constraint.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/logic/> .

# --- 1. The action half: the launching, on-going over an open interval --------
ex:theLaunching
    a logic:Process ;
    logic:occurrentBoundary logic:Open .

# --- 1. The event half: the launch, a completed unitary whole -----------------
ex:theLaunch
    a logic:Event ;
    logic:occurrentBoundary logic:Closed .

# --- 2. Causal parthood: the ignition causally contributes to the launch ------
ex:theIgnition
    a logic:Process ;
    logic:occurrentBoundary logic:Open ;
    logic:causalPartOf ex:theLaunching .

# --- 3. Constitution: the completed launch event is made of the burning --------
ex:theBurning
    a logic:Process ;
    logic:occurrentBoundary logic:Open .

ex:theLaunch
    logic:occurrentConstituent ex:theBurning .
